[{:db/id 17592186157309 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-033d05af-1912-5a6e-86f3-f9dda400af0a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157854 :question/problem "A writer is editing the first draft of a book. On average, there have been $4$ typos per page. What is the probability of finding $2$ typos on the next page? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that typos occur independently and at a constant average rate." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of typos on a page of the book. Since the average rate is $4$ typos per page, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of typos can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =4,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(4).$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{4}^{x}{e}^{-4}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of finding $2$ typos on the next page is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =f(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}{e}^{-4}}{2!} \\\\  & ≈0.147\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186156045 :answer-field/correct 17592186156048 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157311 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-630f14f8-eb57-54c4-9fbf-4988a90b57a0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-630f14f8-eb57-54c4-9fbf-4988a90b57a0" :question/id #uuid "630f14f8-eb57-54c4-9fbf-4988a90b57a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-85394" :question/problem "A telephone exchange receives an average of $7$ calls every $5$ minutes. What is the probability that the exchange will receive at least $5$ calls in the next $5$ minutes? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that calls occur independently and at a constant average rate." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of calls received in the telephone exchange. Since the average rate is $7$ calls every $5$ minutes, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of calls can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =7,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(7).$ \n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{7}^{x}{e}^{-7}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(X\\ge 5),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 5)=1-P(X<5)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{0}{e}^{-7}}{0!}+\\frac{{7}^{1}{e}^{-7}}{1!}+\\frac{{7}^{2}{e}^{-7}}{2!}+\\frac{{7}^{3}{e}^{-7}}{3!}+\\frac{{7}^{4}{e}^{-7}}{4!} \\\\  & ≈0.173\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the probability of receiving at least $5$ calls in the next $5$ minutes is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =1-P(X<5) \\\\  & ≈1-0.173 \\\\  & =0.827\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-80be0045-2641-54de-af08-8fe8e34ad2a8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-80be0045-2641-54de-af08-8fe8e34ad2a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "80be0045-2641-54de-af08-8fe8e34ad2a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3cd87632-86c9-568a-93e5-d7ef69437ccc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b61aade4-803e-5239-8e68-f83d9c20a8cb" "answer-fe83b2b1-31dd-59c3-9890-738677753877" "answer-3cd87632-86c9-568a-93e5-d7ef69437ccc" "answer-7c8348b8-c42d-56b0-b92b-798242f8369b" "answer-4f5cd1e1-b1c5-5fc7-9253-2dc3e4f28a46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b61aade4-803e-5239-8e68-f83d9c20a8cb" :answer/id #uuid "b61aade4-803e-5239-8e68-f83d9c20a8cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.798" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe83b2b1-31dd-59c3-9890-738677753877" :answer/id #uuid "fe83b2b1-31dd-59c3-9890-738677753877" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.812" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cd87632-86c9-568a-93e5-d7ef69437ccc" :answer/id #uuid "3cd87632-86c9-568a-93e5-d7ef69437ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.827" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7c8348b8-c42d-56b0-b92b-798242f8369b" :answer/id #uuid "7c8348b8-c42d-56b0-b92b-798242f8369b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.865" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4f5cd1e1-b1c5-5fc7-9253-2dc3e4f28a46" :answer/id #uuid "4f5cd1e1-b1c5-5fc7-9253-2dc3e4f28a46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.979" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-033d05af-1912-5a6e-86f3-f9dda400af0a" :question/id #uuid "033d05af-1912-5a6e-86f3-f9dda400af0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-131102" :question/problem "A company rents cars to tourists. On average, there have been $3$ rental requests each day. What is the probability that none of the cars are rented the next day? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that rental requests occur independently and at a constant average rate." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of cars rented in a day. Since the average rate is $3$ requests per day, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of rented cars can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =3,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(3).$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{3}^{x}{e}^{-3}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that none of the cars are rented the next day is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0) & =f(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{0}{e}^{-3}}{0!} \\\\  & ≈0.050\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c35bc065-fcec-52cb-96c4-b81be5324354"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c35bc065-fcec-52cb-96c4-b81be5324354" :answer-field/id #uuid "c35bc065-fcec-52cb-96c4-b81be5324354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5546866d-cf0c-5f34-a20b-0d37698b92d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a864749-ecf3-5067-80f4-653b14e5fe85" "answer-d4920049-b97d-5e34-bd87-a602c7c19c73" "answer-5546866d-cf0c-5f34-a20b-0d37698b92d2" "answer-9cc7c554-abbe-5a01-96eb-fd4a8610edf5" "answer-103af267-4448-5f1d-b2c7-5d3a6eb5caa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a864749-ecf3-5067-80f4-653b14e5fe85" :answer/id #uuid "7a864749-ecf3-5067-80f4-653b14e5fe85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.018" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4920049-b97d-5e34-bd87-a602c7c19c73" :answer/id #uuid "d4920049-b97d-5e34-bd87-a602c7c19c73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.034" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5546866d-cf0c-5f34-a20b-0d37698b92d2" :answer/id #uuid "5546866d-cf0c-5f34-a20b-0d37698b92d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.050" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9cc7c554-abbe-5a01-96eb-fd4a8610edf5" :answer/id #uuid "9cc7c554-abbe-5a01-96eb-fd4a8610edf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.122" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-103af267-4448-5f1d-b2c7-5d3a6eb5caa1" :answer/id #uuid "103af267-4448-5f1d-b2c7-5d3a6eb5caa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.132" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157310 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-57e8cbd7-ad98-573e-bd99-c98a3e1a7b22" "question-c5edc979-6530-503b-9c43-a29e848f0191"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-57e8cbd7-ad98-573e-bd99-c98a3e1a7b22" :question/id #uuid "57e8cbd7-ad98-573e-bd99-c98a3e1a7b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-131276" :question/problem "The mean number of bacteria per milliliter of a liquid is $6.$ What is the probability that there will be no more than $3$ bacteria in one milliliter of the liquid? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that bacteria appear independently and at a constant average rate." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of bacteria in one milliliter of the liquid. Since the average rate is $6$ bacteria per milliliter, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of bacteria can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =6,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(6).$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{6}^{x}{e}^{-6}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that at most $3$ bacteria will be found in one milliliter of the liquid is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 3) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{0}{e}^{-6}}{0!}+\\frac{{6}^{1}{e}^{-6}}{1!}+\\frac{{6}^{2}{e}^{-6}}{2!}+\\frac{{6}^{3}{e}^{-6}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.151\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8aa4c72e-18f1-5153-bc4d-2cd8d8207293"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8aa4c72e-18f1-5153-bc4d-2cd8d8207293" :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa4c72e-18f1-5153-bc4d-2cd8d8207293" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0f9e78be-1c05-5746-af99-56ee649b8e69" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ff4f1e3-cf6e-5cd8-8f0c-fc33cf9a7534" "answer-0f9e78be-1c05-5746-af99-56ee649b8e69" "answer-fa8c3282-52ef-59d2-8559-f4a7b0b33e09" "answer-23e97ddf-d3f7-50f6-875a-5463203ee997" "answer-99acdea4-f1d6-5ba9-80fa-995cba142c5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ff4f1e3-cf6e-5cd8-8f0c-fc33cf9a7534" :answer/id #uuid "6ff4f1e3-cf6e-5cd8-8f0c-fc33cf9a7534" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.135" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f9e78be-1c05-5746-af99-56ee649b8e69" :answer/id #uuid "0f9e78be-1c05-5746-af99-56ee649b8e69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.151" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa8c3282-52ef-59d2-8559-f4a7b0b33e09" :answer/id #uuid "fa8c3282-52ef-59d2-8559-f4a7b0b33e09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.156" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23e97ddf-d3f7-50f6-875a-5463203ee997" :answer/id #uuid "23e97ddf-d3f7-50f6-875a-5463203ee997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.221" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-99acdea4-f1d6-5ba9-80fa-995cba142c5c" :answer/id #uuid "99acdea4-f1d6-5ba9-80fa-995cba142c5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.253" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c5edc979-6530-503b-9c43-a29e848f0191" :question/id #uuid "c5edc979-6530-503b-9c43-a29e848f0191" :question/math-academy-id "q-131281" :question/problem "Previous results indicate that, on average, for each batch of transistors, $1$ is defective. What is the probability that in the next batch of transistors, there will be less than $4$ defective transistors? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that defective transistors occur independently and at a constant average rate." :question/worked-solution "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of defective transistors in a batch of transistors. Since the average rate is $1$ defective transistors per batch, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of defective transistors can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =1,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(1).$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{1}^{x}{e}^{-1}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that in the next batch of transistors, there will be less than $4$ defective transistors is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{0}{e}^{-1}}{0!}+\\frac{{1}^{1}{e}^{-1}}{1!}+\\frac{{1}^{2}{e}^{-1}}{2!}+\\frac{{1}^{3}{e}^{-1}}{3!} \\\\  & ≈0.981\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6fbd0a6e-1d11-5207-93f7-e444bfce1656"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6fbd0a6e-1d11-5207-93f7-e444bfce1656" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fbd0a6e-1d11-5207-93f7-e444bfce1656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ed10d1fe-7030-5542-b1f6-229aafd2780f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c22b8e86-37a9-5abd-9b15-d5deb571c1ae" "answer-4e7ef5fa-25a0-50e1-8283-427fee96d7fc" "answer-9b51b374-afa5-5992-b9cf-b6d3ff5216f4" "answer-16527557-36e3-5765-85fe-85ad503bd10f" "answer-ed10d1fe-7030-5542-b1f6-229aafd2780f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c22b8e86-37a9-5abd-9b15-d5deb571c1ae" :answer/id #uuid "c22b8e86-37a9-5abd-9b15-d5deb571c1ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.881" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e7ef5fa-25a0-50e1-8283-427fee96d7fc" :answer/id #uuid "4e7ef5fa-25a0-50e1-8283-427fee96d7fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.890" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b51b374-afa5-5992-b9cf-b6d3ff5216f4" :answer/id #uuid "9b51b374-afa5-5992-b9cf-b6d3ff5216f4" :answer/